
bun is a package manager for node.  It does the same
job as yarn, pnpm, and npm.

pnpm and npm are worthless, because they both require
that a node_modules/ directory be created in each
package directory.  All the names in node_modules/ must
be linked to files in the same physical device as
the package directory, so it is effectively impossible
to manage.  yarn is a bit better, and (allegedly)
can handle symlinks in node_modules/, but it does not
work with Astro unless node_modules/ contains names
which are on the same device.  Allegedly, bun can
handle moving the contents of node_modules/ to a different
physical device, and it works with Astro.
